Attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

honey is a scheduling and reporting wrapper. It depends on, but does not
redistribute, the following work by Perplexity:

  bumblebee
  Copyright Perplexity AI, Inc.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/perplexityai/bumblebee

    - The bumblebee scanner binary provides all package/extension/version
      detection and the exposure-matching engine that honey invokes.
    - The threat_intel exposure catalogs distributed with bumblebee provide
      all supply-chain campaign data that honey matches against.

honey installs bumblebee via `go install` and reads the threat_intel catalogs
from a local checkout of the bumblebee repository at runtime; neither is
included in this repository. All detection capability and threat intelligence
are the work of Perplexity. See https://github.com/perplexityai/bumblebee for
the upstream project, license, and catalog provenance.

honey also offers an OPTIONAL "lens" that, only if the user installs it,
invokes the following work by NVIDIA:

  SkillSpector
  Copyright NVIDIA Corporation
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/NVIDIA/skillspector

    - SkillSpector provides all AI-agent-skill vulnerability detection used by
      honey's optional `lenses/skillspector.sh`.

honey neither installs nor redistributes SkillSpector; the lens is inert
unless the user installs SkillSpector themselves and invokes its CLI at
runtime. All agent-skill detection capability is the work of NVIDIA. See
https://github.com/NVIDIA/skillspector for the upstream project and license.

honey offers two further OPTIONAL vulnerability-scanning lenses that, only if
the user installs the respective tool, invoke:

  osv-scanner
  Copyright Google LLC / the OSV-Scanner authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/google/osv-scanner
    - Used by honey's optional `lenses/osv-scanner.sh` for multi-ecosystem
      lockfile/manifest vulnerability scanning against the OSV database.

  govulncheck
  Copyright The Go Authors
  Licensed under a BSD-style license.
  https://golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck
    - Used by honey's optional `lenses/govulncheck.sh` for Go
      reachability-aware vulnerability scanning against the Go vuln database.

As with the other lenses, honey neither installs nor redistributes these
tools; each lens is inert unless the user installs the tool themselves. All
vulnerability-detection capability is the work of the respective upstream
projects.
